==Enemy==
A strong, hard-hitting enemy that has a standing range on par with [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] but hits progressively farther with each of the three hits of its attack, reaching [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] levels on the third hit. Make sure you have units that can tank its attacks, for its potential pushing power is immense. [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]], [[Evil Cat (Rare Cat)|Evil Cat]], [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and the like are rendered useless by its immunities to freeze and slow.

Casaurian Ahirujo is most dangerous when it has strong peons in front of it, allowing it to chip away at your frontline while not taking too much damage itself.

In later stages such as [[Archaeology 301: Analysis]], [[Burning Sands Area 9]] and [[Sandstorm Area 18]], Ahirujo is no longer the main threat and serves as either a wall to be rushed down as fast as possible before more threatening enemies appear, or a moneybag that helps refill your wallet while fighting said enemies.

==Strategy==
Though they may have wildly different attack ranges and styles, strategy-wise, think of Casaurian Ahirujo as a [[Bore]] that can't be frozen or slowed. [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]], [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Fish Cat]] and optionally [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]] can tank and bring down a lone Ahirujo just as well as against Bore, while [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fried Shrimp Cat]] can do double-duty tanking and weakening, so long as the player has acquired the Blood Fruit from [[Into the Future]], as without them, Ahirujo will be able to tear through one's defense quickly with its full, unweakened stats. Use [[Cat Combo]]s to further improve the efficacy of these units.

Meatshields are important, but [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] have to be at high levels (20+43 and 32 respectively) to endure all three hits from a 100% Ahirujo, so for early players, cheaper options like [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cat]], [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cat]] and [[Kyubey Cat (Rare Cat)|Kyubey Cat]] are preferred unless the Erasers are needed to survive hits from other enemies in the stage. [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]] can also help because Ahirujo tends to move forward ever so slightly after each attack. If you want to try and stall Ahirujo, use Cats such as [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Flamenco Cat]] and/or [[Firecracker Cat (Special Cat)|Macho Firecracker Cat]] because of their chances to [[Dodge Attack|Dodge]] attacks from Red enemies. Even tho they might not help, they are still worth a shot for that duck.

[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] is catered specifically to counter Casaurian Ahirujo, since his Behemoth Slayer and Massive Damage vs. [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] abilities stack multiplicatively, increasing the value by 10x with all [[Blood Fruit]] treasures, which enables Courier to gravely cripple this enemy in a few hits. Before Courier is obtained, [[Bean Cats (Special Cat)|Val Val Cat]] is a decent crowd-controller as it has an effective 91.6k against Casuarian Ahirujo thanks to it's Resistant vs Red and Behemoth Slayer, and it only requires one Behemoth Stone. But Dread Pirate Catley usually suffices enough to not make Val Val Cats necessary in the slightest.

Melee rushers like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] are not effective due to Ahirujo's very strong attack and multi-hit, which will usually cause them to die before they're able to deal significant damage.

