==Trivia==
*"Casaurian" is a portmanteau of [[wikipedia:Cassowary|''Casuarius'']], the genus of birds that cassowaries are in, and ''saurian'', meaning "of or like a lizard".
*The name Ahirujo (アヒルジョー ''Ahirujō'') may be derived from 家鴨 ''ahiru'' ([[wikipedia:Domestic duck|domestic duck]]), イビルジョー ''Ibirujō'' ([[wikia:monsterhunter:Deviljho|Deviljho]]'s Japanese name), ''rojo'' (Spanish for red), ''rouge'' (French for red) and ジョー ''jō'' (jaw, referring to its large beak).
*Ahirujo's frills, beak shape, legs, color scheme and attack animation are highly reminiscent of ''Monster Hunter''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s [[wikia:monsterhunter:Yian Kut-Ku|Yian Kut-Ku]]. Like Ahirujo, Yian Kut-Ku is generally a lower-tier monster encountered early in the game.
**Since Yian Kut-Ku's title is Strange Bird (怪鳥 ''Kaichō''), Ahirujo is likely one of the three Strange Bird Brothers (怪鳥三兄弟 ''Kaichō Sankyōdai'') mentioned in [[Casaurian Darkjo]]'s Japanese description.
*Ahirujo's [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] trait may reference the [[wikipedia:Redhead (bird)|redhead duck]] or [[wikipedia:Ruddy shelduck|ruddy shelduck]].
*[[wikipedia:Foie gras|Foie gras]] is a French "delicacy" made from the fattened liver of a duck or goose. Due to the sheer cruelty of force-feeding and then slaughtering the birds, this dish is banned in many places.
*Although Casaurian Ahirujo, Casaurian Darkjo and [[Ancient Magamojoe]] all have ジョー ''jō'' in their Japanese names, it was romanized inconsistently in English: "jo" for the Casaurians, "joe" for Magamojoe.

